BT /F1 10 Tf 15.00 TL 48 748 Td
(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A single leaky neuron: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 2: An input becomes a voltage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A steady input raises the membrane potential, but the charge also leaks away.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The balance approaches a new resting level; the time constant controls how quickly) Tj T*
(it gets there.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Differential equation: tau * dV/dt = -\(V - Vrest\) + R*I. Numerical method: forward) Tj T*
(Euler, dt = 0.1 ms. At each step, V += \(-\(V+65\)+10*I\)/tau * 0.1. Equilibrium: Vrest) Tj T*
(+ R*I. There is no stochastic input.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The time constant divides the voltage's rate of change. A larger tau slows the) Tj T*
(approach, while the equilibrium Vrest + RI remains the same. With 1 nA and R = 10) Tj T*
(Mohm, that equilibrium is -55 mV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Leak: The tendency for the membrane voltage to move back toward rest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Integration: Input and leak together determine how voltage changes over time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Steady input: A constant current pushes the voltage toward Vrest + RI.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Axon: The output path that carries the neuron's signal away from its cell body.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
