(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A single leaky neuron: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 3: A threshold changes everything.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When the membrane reaches -50 mV, our model emits a spike and resets to -65 mV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A two-millisecond refractory interval follows, then the membrane begins integrating) Tj T*
(again.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After the Euler voltage update, if V >= -50 mV: increment spike count; set V = -65) Tj T*
(mV; set refractory timer = 2 ms. While that timer is positive, decrement it by dt) Tj T*
(\(clamped at zero\) and hold V = -65 mV. A +20 mV graphical marker records an event,) Tj T*
(not an action-potential waveform.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An input of 1 nA approaches -55 mV, below the -50 mV threshold. Inputs greater than) Tj T*
(1.5 nA can reach the threshold in this model. The spike marker at +20 mV is a) Tj T*
(drawing convention, not a biological action-potential waveform.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Threshold: The voltage at which the model emits a spike: -50 mV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Spike: A discrete output event, drawn as a sharp line in the trace.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reset: After a spike, voltage returns to -65 mV before integration resumes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
