BT /F1 10 Tf 15.00 TL 48 748 Td
(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A single leaky neuron: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 4: More input. A faster rhythm.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Stronger input shortens the journey to threshold, so the neuron fires more often.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Our simulation produced 33 spikes at 2 nA and 63 spikes at 3 nA in the first 1 s) Tj T*
(\(0?1000 ms\); the tags and the plot count the same window.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reference targets measured over 1000 ms at tau=20 ms: I=0 nA -> 0 spikes; I=1 nA ->) Tj T*
(0 spikes; I=2 nA -> 33 spikes; I=3 nA -> 63 spikes. Approximate continuous-model) Tj T*
(rate for I>1.5 nA: f=1000/\(tau*ln\(R*I/\(R*I-15\)\)+2\) Hz. Finite observation time and) Tj T*
(discrete Euler updates cause small differences from this formula. Passing numerical) Tj T*
(agreement is not validation against a published paper or biological data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The charging time depends on a logarithm, and every spike adds a refractory) Tj T*
(interval. Our simulation gives 33 spikes at 2 nA and 63 at 3 nA in the first 1 s) Tj T*
(\(0?1000 ms\), matching the checked Python reference. This is numerical agreement) Tj T*
(with our reference model, not validation against a research paper or biological) Tj T*
(data. The analytic expression is approximate for the discrete model.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Firing rate: Spikes counted in the first 1 s \(0?1000 ms\) of a run, per second.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Interspike interval: Time between two spike events; shorter intervals mean a faster) Tj T*
(rhythm.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Threshold: The same -50 mV boundary, reached faster under stronger input.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
